From 7f0a44e9485bc4953c117ba2069b09d925c45652 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 16:56:29 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 403/453] fix(kanban): share one remote inventory per store
 state; best-effort snapshot [daveey]

_remote_links rebuilt the full replica + receipt projection on every call:
twice per /api/profiles/sessions request (kanban counts, then the
chat-closeout plugin), plus once per concurrent poll, at ~0.2-0.7 s each.

- _remote_links: cached per origin scope for _CACHE_TTL_S while no store it
  reads changed (boards, hub replica, origin ledger; state.db alias tips
  are bounded by the TTL), single-flight so concurrent readers wait for the
  running projection. Failures are never cached.
- _legacy_remote_links: the origin-work.db snapshot is written only when
  the inventory changed, and a failed write (database is locked) is logged
  instead of failing the read. It raised out of annotate_kanban_activity
  and marked every sidebar row kanban_unknown (errors.log, twice on
  2026-10-26). _remote_snapshot itself still propagates write failures.

Tests: new test_kanban_remote_inventory_cache.py (shared projection,
store-change and TTL invalidation, single-flight via an Event-gated
projection, failures not cached, locked snapshot write, write-once); the
four behaviour cases are red on base. test_kanban_local_receipt_authority
re-stubs ledger.project without changing any store, so it resets the cache
before those reads.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 7f0a44e9485bc4953c117ba2069b09d925c45652)
